      en: "Lake Muzairib is a shallow seasonal lake in southwestern Syria, near Daraa. Its area ranges from 10 km² in wet years to near dryness during droughts. The lake is fed by groundwater and winter rainfall. It serves as a crucial stopover for migratory birds, including flamingos and pelicans. Surrounding lands are used for agriculture, mainly cereals and vegetables. During Roman times, it was incorporated into an irrigation network. Currently, the lake faces threats from over-extraction of water and fertilizer runoff. Conservation efforts are minimal due to regional instability.",
